## 4. Testing Guidelines

- **Frameworks:** JUnit 5 (`org.junit.jupiter.api.*`) and Mockito (`org.mockito.*`).
- **Testing Approach:**
  - Write unit tests for all Service layers, Repositories, and Controller layers.
  - Always cover **both success and failure/exception scenarios**.
  - Use `@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)` for service unit tests.
  - Follow the **Given-When-Then** (or AAA: Arrange-Act-Assert) structure.

```java
@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)
class AlarmServiceImplTest {

    @Mock
    private AlarmRepository alarmRepository;

    @InjectMocks
    private AlarmServiceImpl alarmService;

    @Test
    @DisplayName("Should return alarm DTO when valid alarm ID is provided")
    void getAlarmById_Success() {
        // Given
        String alarmId = "ALM-101";
        Alarm alarm = new Alarm(alarmId, "CRITICAL", "High Temperature");
        when(alarmRepository.findById(alarmId)).thenReturn(Optional.of(alarm));

        // When
        AlarmResponseDto result = alarmService.findAlarmById(alarmId);

        // Then
        assertThat(result).isNotNull();
        assertThat(result.id()).isEqualTo(alarmId);
        verify(alarmRepository, times(1)).findById(alarmId);
    }

    @Test
    @DisplayName("Should throw AlarmNotFoundException when alarm ID does not exist")
    void getAlarmById_NotFound_ThrowsException() {
        // Given
        String alarmId = "INVALID-ID";
        when(alarmRepository.findById(alarmId)).thenReturn(Optional.empty());

        // When & Then
        assertThrows(AlarmNotFoundException.class, () -> alarmService.findAlarmById(alarmId));
        verify(alarmRepository, times(1)).findById(alarmId);
    }
}
```

